notes.content:
Meme Survivors was planned as a project with tons of maps, heroes, and everything else, but during development it became clear that there’s little demand for it and not much point in carrying on…

But I couldn’t leave it as it was.
So:

— A complete redesign of the Steam page and the main menu;
— A shift to a single-location concept with gameplay structured as two 30-minute runs;
— Full support for controllers and keyboard;
— Replacement of sounds and music;
— Bug fixes and rebalancing;
— Improved UI;
— A hero-purchase system;
— 10 achievements.

And a bunch of other stuff that’s not even worth listing.
Yes, only a few people have played—and probably will play—but I’m not ashamed of the final result, because the core goal—time-killing and distraction—is achieved.

Have fun, friends!
See you in other projects.

Memes for the world!
